<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Czechoslovak Legion</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1914–1920</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Czechoslovak <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/legion">Legion</a> was a force of Czech and Slovak volunteers, many of them former prisoners of war, who fought for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>, above all in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>. In May 1918, while travelling east along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trans-siberian-railway">Trans-Siberian Railway</a> to reach <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, its troops revolted against the Bolsheviks and seized much of the railway, helping to set off the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-civil-war">Russian Civil War</a>. They were evacuated through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vladivostok">Vladivostok</a> by 1920.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/czechoslovak-legion.jpg" alt="Czechoslovak Legion" width="320" height="334" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coat_of_arms_of_the_Czechoslovak_Legion.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
